 "dha-license-healthcare-professionals-dubai": {
  "info_one": "<h3>What it takes to get your DHA license</h3>\n<p>You need a DHA license to work as a physician, dentist, nurse, midwife, pharmacist or allied health professional at a facility licensed by the Dubai Health Authority.</p>",
  "info_two": "<h3>Checking Your Eligibility</h3><p>DHA assesses your qualifications and experience against the Unified Healthcare Professional Qualification Requirements (PQR) for your title. For Specialist and Consultant titles, the experience required also depends on the PQR tier of the country where you trained. Before you apply, we check your title and experience against the PQR, so you apply for a title you qualify for. The minimum for common titles:</p><ul><li>General Practitioner: the internship year, then two years in clinical practice</li><li>General Dentist: the internship, then two years of practice</li><li>Registered Nurse: a bachelor's degree in nursing; no minimum experience</li><li>Pharmacist: two years after qualifying, not counting work for pharmaceutical companies or in sales</li></ul><p>Most allied health titles need one to four years.</p><h3>Preparing Your Application in Sheryan</h3><p>DHA licensing runs through Sheryan, the DHA licensing system. You open your application there, and DataFlow verifies your documents directly with the institutions that issued them. We prepare your documents, submit your application and follow your DataFlow verification, keeping you informed of what is outstanding at each stage.</p><h3>Passing the DHA Exam</h3><p>Most titles sit the DHA licensing exam at a Prometric centre. Depending on your title, the assessment can be written, oral or an OSCE, and it is held in English. The PQR allows three attempts across the UAE health authorities; after three failed attempts, you have one final attempt with a different authority. We guide you on the format for your title before you book.</p><h3>Checking for an Exam Exemption</h3><p>The PQR exempts UAE nationals and holders of listed international qualifications or registrations, such as UK and US boards, PLAB, USMLE or NCLEX. If you already hold a valid DOH, MOHAP or SHA license, you can apply to DHA for the same title with an exam exemption, with a good standing certificate and a full DataFlow report. We confirm whether an exemption applies to you before you book an exam.</p><h3>Activating and Keeping Your License</h3><p>DHA issues your registration, often called the eligibility letter, which is valid for one year. Your license becomes active when a DHA-licensed facility employs you and <a href=\"https://alphahmc.com/services/activate-your-uae-healthcare-license\">activates it</a>. Every year you complete continuing education in your specialty: 40 CME credits for physicians and dentists, 20 for nurses and pharmacists, and 10 for allied health professionals. Physicians and dentists in surgical specialties also submit a surgical logbook every two years for renewal.</p><h3>Avoiding Delays</h3><ul><li>Check your time out of practice. A break of more than three years means completing CME credits and a period of training in an approved setting, and you still sit the exam. Non-UAE nationals cannot apply after a break of more than five years.</li><li>Use an exemption while it applies. Exemptions do not apply after more than two years out of practice.</li><li>Plan around the eligibility letter. It is valid for one year, so your employer needs to activate your license within that time.</li></ul><p>A license from DOH or MOHAP does not cover Dubai. Working in Abu Dhabi or the Northern Emirates instead? See <a href=\"https://alphahmc.com/service-packages/healthcare-professional-licensing-uae\">which UAE license you need</a>. Already licensed in another emirate? See <a href=\"https://alphahmc.com/services/healthcare-professional-license-transfer\">license transfers between authorities</a>. Official requirements: <a href=\"https://www.dha.gov.ae\">Dubai Health Authority</a>.</p>"
 },
 "doh-license-healthcare-professionals-abu-dhabi": {
  "info_one": "<h3>What it takes to get your DOH license</h3>\n<p>You need a DOH license to practise as a physician, dentist, nurse, midwife, pharmacist or allied health professional anywhere in the Emirate of Abu Dhabi.</p>",
  "info_two": "<h3>Checking Your Eligibility</h3><p>The department checks your qualifications and experience against the Unified Healthcare Professional Qualification Requirements (PQR) for your title. Specialist and Consultant requirements depend on the PQR tier of the country where you trained, and physicians trained in Tier 3 countries cannot hold the Consultant title. Before you apply, we check your title against the PQR, so you apply for a title you qualify for. The minimum for common titles:</p><ul><li>General Practitioner: the internship year, then two years in clinical practice</li><li>General Dentist: the internship, then two years of practice</li><li>Registered Nurse: a bachelor's degree in nursing; no minimum experience</li><li>Pharmacist: two years after qualifying, not counting work for pharmaceutical companies or in sales</li></ul><h3>Preparing Your Application on TAMM</h3><p>You apply for a DOH license through TAMM, the Abu Dhabi government services platform. DataFlow confirms your degrees, experience, licenses and good standing with the institutions that issued them. We prepare your documents for DataFlow, file your application on TAMM and follow it through verification, keeping you informed of what is outstanding.</p><h3>Passing the DOH Exam</h3><p>If your title requires it, you book the DOH licensing exam with Pearson VUE from your TAMM account. We guide you through the booking and the exam requirements for your title, so you sit it at the right point in your application.</p><h3>Checking for an Exam Exemption</h3><p>You may not need the exam if you are a UAE national, if you hold a qualification or registration on the PQR lists, such as US or UK board certification, PLAB, USMLE or NCLEX, or if you already hold a valid DHA, MOHAP or SHA license for the same title with a good standing certificate and a full DataFlow report. We confirm whether an exemption applies to you before you book an exam.</p><h3>Moving From DHA or MOHAP</h3><p>Apply to DOH for a transfer on TAMM while your current license is still valid. Your DataFlow report is transferred to DOH, which may ask for more verification, and specialist titles also need your residency programme documents. Your Abu Dhabi employer then activates the license. Most transfers take 4 to 6 weeks. See <a href=\"https://alphahmc.com/services/healthcare-professional-license-transfer\">license transfers between authorities</a>.</p><h3>Activating and Keeping Your License</h3><p>Once the department confirms you are eligible for the title, your license becomes active when a licensed facility in Abu Dhabi employs you and <a href=\"https://alphahmc.com/services/activate-your-uae-healthcare-license\">activates it</a>. Every year you complete continuing education in your specialty: 40 CME credits for physicians and dentists, 20 for nurses and pharmacists, and 10 for allied health professionals. Surgical specialists also submit a logbook every two years for renewal.</p><h3>Avoiding Delays</h3><ul><li>Get a recent good standing certificate. It must come from the regulator where you last practised and be no more than six months old when you apply.</li><li>Check your time out of practice. After more than three years, the PQR requires CME credits and a training period in an approved setting. Non-UAE nationals cannot apply after more than five years away.</li><li>Use an exemption while it applies. No exemption applies after more than two years out of practice.</li></ul><p>The license is issued by the <a href=\"https://www.doh.gov.ae\">Department of Health Abu Dhabi</a>; a DHA or MOHAP license does not cover Abu Dhabi. Not sure which authority applies to you? <a href=\"https://alphahmc.com/service-packages/healthcare-professional-licensing-uae\">Compare DHA, DOH and MOHAP</a>.</p>"
 },
 "mohap-license-healthcare-professionals": {
  "info_one": "<h3>What it takes to get your MOHAP license</h3>\n<p>You need a MOHAP license to practise as a physician, dentist, nurse, midwife, pharmacist or allied health professional in Ajman, Umm Al Quwain, Ras Al Khaimah or Fujairah.</p>",
  "info_two": "<h3>Checking Your Eligibility</h3><p>Your eligibility depends on your title. The ministry assesses your qualifications and experience against the Unified Healthcare Professional Qualification Requirements (PQR); for Specialist and Consultant titles, the PQR tier of the country where you trained also counts, and physicians trained in Tier 3 countries cannot hold the Consultant title. We review your documents against the PQR first, so your application matches the title you can hold. Common titles need:</p><ul><li>General Practitioner: the internship year, then two years in clinical practice</li><li>General Dentist: the internship, then two years of practice</li><li>Registered Nurse: a bachelor's degree in nursing; no minimum experience</li><li>Pharmacist: two years after qualifying, not counting work for pharmaceutical companies or in sales</li></ul><h3>Preparing Your Application on the MOHAP Portal</h3><p>Applications go through the ministry portal, using the <a href=\"https://mohap.gov.ae/en/w/licensing-or-re-licensing-of-health-professional\">licensing or re-licensing of health professional</a> service. DataFlow confirms your degrees, experience, licenses and good standing with the institutions that issued them. We get your documents ready for DataFlow, submit the application and track the verification, so you always know what is still needed.</p><h3>Passing the MOHAP Exam</h3><p>Titles that need an exam sit the ministry licensing exam with Prometric. We explain the requirements for your title and help you book, so the exam fits the timing of your application.</p><h3>Checking for an Exam Exemption</h3><p>Three groups may be exempt from the exam: UAE nationals; holders of a qualification or registration on the PQR lists, such as US or UK board certification, PLAB, USMLE or NCLEX; and professionals who already hold a valid DHA, DOH or SHA license for the same title, with a good standing certificate and a full DataFlow report. We check your case against these rules before you register for the exam.</p><h3>Moving From DHA or DOH</h3><p>Apply to MOHAP for a transfer while your current license is still valid. Your DataFlow report is transferred to MOHAP, which may ask for more verification. Your new employer then activates the license. Most transfers take 3 to 5 weeks. See <a href=\"https://alphahmc.com/services/healthcare-professional-license-transfer\">license transfers between authorities</a>.</p><h3>Activating and Keeping Your License</h3><p>After the ministry confirms your eligibility, the license is activated by your employer: a licensed facility in the Northern Emirates employs you and <a href=\"https://alphahmc.com/services/activate-your-uae-healthcare-license\">activates it</a>. Every year you complete continuing education in your specialty: 40 CME credits for physicians and dentists, 20 for nurses and pharmacists, and 10 for allied health professionals. Surgical specialists also submit a logbook every two years for renewal.</p><h3>Avoiding Delays</h3><ul><li>Time your good standing certificate. It has to come from the regulator where you last practised, dated no more than six months before you apply.</li><li>Account for any career break. A break of more than three years means CME credits and a training period in an approved setting under the PQR, and non-UAE nationals cannot apply after five years away.</li><li>Claim an exemption early. Once you have been out of practice for more than two years, no exemption applies.</li></ul><p>The license is issued by the <a href=\"https://mohap.gov.ae\">Ministry of Health and Prevention</a>. Dubai (DHA), Abu Dhabi (DOH) and Sharjah (SHA) license their own healthcare professionals, so a MOHAP license does not cover them. Not sure which authority applies to you? <a href=\"https://alphahmc.com/service-packages/healthcare-professional-licensing-uae\">Compare DHA, DOH and MOHAP</a>.</p>"
 }
